WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.190
- He rolled into our lives with dimples

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:04.200
and a wrestling singlet, yeah he did.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.370
Over 30 years ago in "Saved By The Bell",

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:08.280
you can see him now on "Access Hollywood"

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.800
as well as in the new
"Saved By The Bell" reboot,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.793
coming to Peacock, please
welcome Mario Lopez!

00:00:15.238 --> 00:00:20.238
(jazzy music)
(audience clapping)

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.670
Sorry we have to sit so far apart.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.700
I have one bone to pick with you.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.680
- Okay.
- So like,

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.030
with "Saved By The Bell" reboot,

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:35.870
I know that somebody had
to sing the theme song.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:37.120
- Yes.
- Yeah, who was that?

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.470
- You know what, we
actually had Lil Yachty.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.580
- Okay, fine. That's fine.
(laughing)

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:43.710
- Can I tell you something Kelly though?

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.138
- I would have totally done it.

00:00:45.138 --> 00:00:47.180
- Okay.
- I just sang the whole thing

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.730
before you came out here with Jesse.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.110
- I was hearing you backstage.
- Okay.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:51.640
- You know I love you, you
know you're my favorite.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.160
- I'm just saying, it
would have been amazing.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.027
- I know you would have killed it.

00:00:54.027 --> 00:00:55.140
- Lil Yachty's probably amazing.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.890
- I always tell everyone 'cause you know,

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.610
first of all, thank you so
much for filling in for me

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.560
on my radio show, we did the countdown.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.040
Everyone over at "On
With Mario" loves you.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.370
You know, we're big, big fans.

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:06.100
But I always say, I feel
sorry for the other artists

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.050
when you do the Kellyoke's,

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:08.570
'cause you do their songs so much better.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:09.760
- Oh, you're-
- I'm not lying.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:11.600
You usually take it next
level and it's so much better.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:12.840
Oh my God, I would by that one.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.010
- Sometimes it doesn't work.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:15.520
My favorite thing that
someone's ever said to me,

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:16.940
Garth was actually, Garth
Brooks was on the show

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:17.997
and he goes, "Is there any song,

00:01:17.997 --> 00:01:19.710
"like any genre you wouldn't go near?"

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:22.930
And I was like, "There are
genres I shouldn't go near."

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:24.410
But I do it.

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:25.750
- No, no, you're killin' 'em all.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.239
- I love music.
- I know.

00:01:27.239 --> 00:01:28.072
- So that's what's cool about your job too

00:01:28.072 --> 00:01:29.370
you get to like, celebrate all music.

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:30.290
- Yes, I love music too.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:31.660
I love music, I love entertainment

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:32.520
that's why I love doing
"Access Hollywood".

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:34.240
- How has it been? Because COVID's weird.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:35.257
So how's it been doing the radio show,

00:01:35.257 --> 00:01:36.170
"Access Hollywood", all of it?

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:37.010
- You know what?

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:39.280
We really haven't stopped, to be honest.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:40.870
So we did a little bit at home.

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:43.610
I was shooting out in my
backyard with "Access Hollywood".

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:45.630
- I had to do it out of my
backyard for a while too.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:46.463
- Yeah, for a little while,

00:01:46.463 --> 00:01:48.790
but then we were the first
show, I believe, on the lot,

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:50.310
back with "Access", which is great.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.143
Which is nice,

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:52.900
because we're celebrating
our 25 year anniversary

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:54.070
- Wow!
- And we're really excited

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:54.950
over there about that.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.760
And then, "On With Mario", with the show,

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.120
we do it on the lot as well

00:01:58.120 --> 00:01:59.440
so everything's sort of
consolidated right here,

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:00.970
so we've kind of kept on going.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:03.457
Between that, and then I
did my Christmas movie,

00:02:03.457 --> 00:02:05.724
"Feliz Navidad"
- Yes, that's amazing.

00:02:05.724 --> 00:02:07.250
- over in Nevada, so I've
been keeping really busy.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.150
And the new "Saved By The Bell", so yeah.

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.000
- That's amazing.

